- Raise minLength to avoid noisy short texts (e.g., minLength: 10–15). For very short texts, skip detection and fall back to the user/session default.
- Session-level caching (high ROI):
  - Persist “current session language + confidence” in Redis with TTL (e.g., 30–60 minutes). If confidence is high and messages are frequent, skip re-detecting every message; re-check only on big content changes or every N messages.
- Per-text caching:
  - Cache normalized text → lang in Redis with a short TTL (5–10 min). Hit rate varies, but it helps during bursts and repeated phrases.

Redis (fit your 7.0 + LRU preference)
- Configure a hard cap and eviction:
